      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "@{5a015331a6fd0876a51d5148|full_name}: I hope the knuckles controller also allows this but I figured for those few who knew sign language they could at least communicate better without it using this system. \n\nThis is also why I suggested a separate gesture-recognition system that displays text or maybe an audible text-to-speech voice to allow people to hear what they're trying to sign. I can see it being janky in many cases but better than nothing. I'm not sure if they'd take the time to develop such a system for a small percentage of users so maybe we'll have to wait and see if the knuckles controller gets implemented.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5a6faa876feffe4d02a0629d",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5a6c4d4edb821e1569d46de3",
        "alias": "Continuing Ant",
        "aliasID": "65ba0267ed6eefce4c0abe52",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/04fd5a4de619c92e46f8194f71a82698.png",
        "created": "2018-01-27T09:58:38.732Z",
        "name": "Darksunrise",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-01-29T23:13:11.775Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a5d66760c8f72447a01beef",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "That would take a lot of development resources, for an extremely marginal use case. As much as I do believe it would be a nice option to have, resources would be far better spent in making many of the other much-needed features that everyone would benefit from. A system where you could type out what you wanted to say, and it would appear as floating text above your head (probably only for a few seconds before fading away) would not only solve the problem of needing sign language, it would allow others who DON'T know sign language to understand you too. Not to mention it could be used by anyone who doesn't have a microphone.\n\nEDIT: Not sure if there are already any text chat capabilities built in. If so, then that would probably be adequate, or at least an easily expandable solution.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5a7208dec62a345bf0d8b250",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5a60e3832478a072c83fa7ce",
        "alias": "Pink Reindeer",
        "aliasID": "65ba0213ed6eefce4c025aef",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": "https://canny.io/images/87b8dde596737c70bce64a542ea07379.jpg",
        "created": "2018-01-18T18:12:19.205Z",
        "name": "Lhun",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-01-31T18:20:14.206Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": null,
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5a5d66760c8f72447a01beef",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "value": "A much easier to implement feature for people hard of hearing (but unfortunately not as useful for those hard of speaking) would be a client side speech to text bubble. The avatar would only need a single poly instanced speech bubble with a shapeblend to draw the words out once confirmed. This would also allow people to \"speak\" without their voice, and it would be arbitrary to then enable speech to text, which would allow people to change their voice automatically. Both options are something the game needs.\n\nThe japanese language (unfortunate for english speakers!) provides a much better option for text input due to the way it's structured that is incredibly rapid in vr. \n\nhttps://github.com/yutokun/VR-Text-Input\n\nI wish something existed for english in the same way.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
