      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Having access to more of the inputs on the controllers for additional sign language guestures would be awesome.\nIt would also be nice having some way of identifying \"Hey! I don't speak or hear! I sign!\".\nBut I think that third point there for machine translation of sign is a very hard task to do.  Still, I like the broad feature request so I've upvoted :D",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-16T02:41:58.219Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A dedicated and toggleable mode for sign language users that allows them to have more hand gestures available to them for more accurate signing. \n\n* When toggling the mode on in the Escape menu, pressing the push-to-talk button on their controllers would bring up a UI that lets them see every gesture available and quickly pick them for faster signing. \n* When the push-to-talk (or in this case push-to-sign) button is held, there's also a hand symbol instead of a speaker symbol next to their nametag to let everyone know they're trying to communicate.\n* Additionally, if there were a way to develop a system that recognized signing and displayed words in front of or above the avatar to allow non-ASL users to understand them, that'd be a great feature to bridge some communication barriers.",
